0..77 Comment "//! Confluence certificates as paths in a presented type, and univalence over"
78..99 Comment "//! the types of them"
100..177 Comment "//! [Program-2013-homotopy_type_theory_univalent_foundations_mathematics], §"
178..191 Comment "//! 2.10, and"
192..270 Comment "//! [Behr-2022-tracelet_hopf_algebras_decomposition_spaces_extended_abstract]."
271..350 Comment "//! The critical pair of the presented integers at `S(P(S(x)))` joins at `S(x)`"
351..429 Comment "//! two ways, and each way is a certificate: a path from the peak to the join."
430..507 Comment "//! The two are one path, so certificate identity is an identification in the"
508..581 Comment "//! presented type rather than a relation beside it; certificates no rule"
582..662 Comment "//! relates stay apart (the pathological twin). Two boundaries that convert have"
663..738 Comment "//! certificate types that `ua` makes one, and a consumer of one boundary\'s"
739..792 Comment "//! certificates is carried to the other\'s unchanged."
793..796 Comment "//!"
797..879 Comment "//! - cites: [Program-2013-homotopy_type_theory_univalent_foundations_mathematics]"
880..966 Comment "//! - cites: [Behr-2022-tracelet_hopf_algebras_decomposition_spaces_extended_abstract]"
967..970 Comment "//!"
971..1169 Comment "//! [Program-2013-homotopy_type_theory_univalent_foundations_mathematics]: https://arxiv.org/abs/1308.0729 \"Univalent Foundations Program, Homotopy Type Theory: Univalent Foundations of Mathematics\""
1170..1350 Comment "//! [Behr-2022-tracelet_hopf_algebras_decomposition_spaces_extended_abstract]: https://doi.org/10.4204/EPTCS.372.23 \"Behr and Kock, Tracelet Hopf Algebras and Decomposition Spaces\""
